MDM Migration End User Guide
Mac users completing a company management migration  |  MDM enrollment migration and Platform SSO completion

What this tool does
MDM Migration refreshes the company management registration on the Mac and completes the company sign-in setup. The workflow guides the user through required macOS prompts, automatically installs the required company sign-in component when it is missing, and performs cleanup when finished.

 
Before you begin
• Save open work.
• Stay signed in to the Mac.
• Connect to a reliable, approved network.
• Disconnect GlobalProtect VPN if it is connected.
• Keep the Mac awake and connected to the internet.
• Have the normal Mac username and password available.
Important
Do not select Enrollment Complete until macOS has finished every enrollment prompt.

 
Complete the migration
1. Open MDM Migration from Self Service.
2. Read the preparation message and select Continue.
3. If Network Change Required appears, connect to an approved network and select Check Again.
4. If VPN Disconnect Required appears, disconnect GlobalProtect, stay connected to the approved network, and select Check Again.
5. Wait while the Mac is prepared. The required company sign-in component may be installed automatically during this step. Do not close the preparation window.
6. Complete every macOS enrollment prompt. Enter the normal Mac username and password if requested, complete company sign-in, and approve management enrollment.
7. After macOS indicates enrollment is finished, return to the Complete Management Enrollment window and select Enrollment Complete.
8. Wait while the tool validates enrollment, restores the normal account configuration, and completes company sign-in setup.
9. When Refresh Complete appears, select OK. The Mac can then be used normally.
If enrollment needs to be reopened
In the Complete Management Enrollment window, select Reopen Enrollment. Finish the remaining macOS prompts, then return to the tool and select Enrollment Complete.
What the user may see
Message

What it means

What to do

Network Change Required
The current network cannot be used for the migration.
Connect to an approved network and select Check Again.
VPN Disconnect Required
GlobalProtect or another detected VPN connection is active.
Disconnect VPN and select Check Again.
Refresh Needs Attention
A required validation, component installation, or company sign-in step could not be completed.
Read the message, select OK, and follow the recommended action. Contact the Service Desk if the issue continues.
Refresh Complete
Management enrollment and account cleanup were validated.
Select OK and continue working normally.
 
If the workflow is canceled
The tool removes temporary account changes during cleanup. The migration can be started again from Self Service when the Mac is ready.
When to contact the Service Desk
• The same failure message appears after running the tool again.
• The enrollment window does not open.
• The company sign-in component cannot be installed or company sign-in setup does not complete.
• The Mac remains unenrolled after all macOS prompts were completed.
• The tool reports that account cleanup could not be verified.
Helpful information to provide
• The exact message displayed by the tool.
• Whether the Mac was connected to VPN.
• Whether all macOS enrollment prompts completed.
• The approximate point where the workflow stopped.
Privacy reminder
Do not send passwords, verification codes, or screenshots containing sensitive personal or company information.

 
